[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557187196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557187196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557187196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ya5R8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T15:08:42Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T15:08:42Z","body":"The choice to make `String(char *)` only accept Latin1 is by design as a performance benefit, but needs to be communicated better to avoid issues","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557187196/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557236366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557236366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557236366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YbFSO","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T15:36:54Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T15:38:49Z","body":"> The choice to make `String(char *)` only accept Latin1 is by design as a performance benefit, but needs to be communicated better to avoid issues\n\nI guessed as much (though it doesn't appear to be documented).\n\nThe actual performance gain for this decision should be tested. I don't think it has a big impact, and correctness is always more important than performance.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557236366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557263987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557263987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557263987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YbMBz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T15:53:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T15:53:24Z","body":"I agree, there was talk of adding a check for correctness as well, but *almost all* string literals are latin1 so that's important to keep in mind as well, or rather ASCII","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557263987/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557421598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557421598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557421598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ybyge","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T17:22:10Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T17:24:09Z","body":"I think making people extra aware of that raw strings are parsed as latin1 is important, and do a survey of how many actual string sequences in the codebase are using other encodings, either using `String::utf8` or `U\"...\"`, because I feel that changing the standard constructor (which would also break compatibility at least partially as this is also exposed to GDExtension) would risk worsening performance\n\nHaving a slight performance drop to parse utf8 (I'd say it's almost guaranteed that it would hurt performance at least somewhat, though might be barely noticeable) would be bad IMO if it would be essentially unused, which I suspect is the case in the existing codebase. Most cases, like names, types, etc. are strictly ASCII, and outside of certain string literals like property hints (using special characters like the degree symbol) we *shouldn't* be using non-ASCII literals generally I'd say, not just a matter of that we aren't\n\nTl;dr; If something like 90% or more of the literals in the codebase are ASCII any drop in performance for swapping to utf8 would be a negative, as that feature would be nigh unused ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557421598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557434091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557434091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557434091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yb1jr","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T17:31:22Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T17:31:45Z","body":"> Tl;dr; If something like 90% or more of the literals in the codebase are ASCII any drop in performance for swapping to utf8 would be a negative, as that feature would be nigh unused\n\nI agree, that's why I think just statically checking for non-ASCII in string literals would be best (and disallowing the default string constructor for anything else, forcing them to call `String::utf8()` or something else explicitly). That would give us the best of both worlds.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557434091/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557448878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557448878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557448878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yb5Ku","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T17:41:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T17:41:23Z","body":"Agreed, handling things with literals specially would be very useful, most if not all dynamic input is processed as utf8 already, with a few exceptions that should probably use the explicit case of `ascii` instead to make things explicit ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557448878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557451367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557451367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557451367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yb5xn","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T17:42:50Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T17:43:29Z","body":"Does anyone has some data on this ? Like how many static strings are parsed in the codebase, and what's the average size for them. Because if we're talking 20 bytes string, the difference between these should be very small. I'm not even sure parse utf8 parsing only ascii would ba that slow. But we can probably measure that. I have not access to my computer for some time, but it would be nice to gather those metrics, to avoid guessing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557451367/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557494928","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2557494928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2557494928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YcEaQ","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T18:13:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T18:13:23Z","body":"Not sure if there's any data, but you can estimate amount of string literals by checking translation files (`editor/translations`), it won't include console only error messages and some other stuff, but should give a lower bound. And since engine UI translation is done via `po` files, all string literals in the code in general are in English (ASCII only), there are only few special cases using non ASCII characters (`µs`, `•`, `⚠`, `×`, `±`, box drawing characters, font preview sample strings, few special strings for pseudolocalizations).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557494928/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564688199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641#issuecomment-2564688199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100641","id":2564688199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y3glH","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T11:05:17Z","updated_at":"2024-12-29T11:05:17Z","body":"I think we can sefely ignore all files from `po` files, as they uses `parse_utf8` already anyway, this would not change anything for them.\n\nI did some quick benchmarking for the cost of `parse_utf8` vs `parse_latin`.\nI tested 2 kind of strings, long ones around (500 bytes) to amortize the startup cost (aka memory allocation), and short ones (around 20 bytes), probably more relevant to static string in the codebase. (parse_utf8_PR is the implementation from [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99826))\n\n| Function | Cycles (Long) | Cycles (Short)|\n| :---------------- | :------: | :----: |\n| `latin1`|   5 | 39 |\n| `parse_utf8`           |   11 | 60 |\n| `parse_utf8_PR`    |  8.5| 55 |\n\nSo in the case of small strings, we're talking about 200-300 cycles difference per string. This is not nothing, but if you happen to do it 50 times in a frame, this is a 10k cycles budget. \nThe right question now is, is this cost too much to remove some unlikely errors ? (might be, might not be).\nIf those static strings are not transformed into Strings every frame, but only once on startup, then I think we should parse_utf8 by default, as the difference would not be noticeable, even for thousands of those. \n\nIf anyone wants to test this, here is the code, to drop in `Main::iteration` somewhere ( maybe need some tuning for the rdtsc intrinsics depending on your compiler)\n```\nconst char mySuperString[] = \"Does anyone has some ?\";\n\nstatic uint64_t latin = 0;\nstatic uint64_t utf = 0;\nstatic uint64_t iterations = 0;\n\n++iterations;\nuint64_t start = __rdtsc();\nString normalString(mySuperString);\nuint64_t end = __rdtsc();\nString utfString;\nutfString.parse_utf8(mySuperString);\nuint64_t utfEnd = __rdtsc();\n\nlatin += end - start;\nutf += utfEnd - end;\n\nreal_t latins = (real_t)(latin / iterations);\nreal_t utfs   = (real_t)(utf / iterations);\nuint32_t size = sizeof(mySuperString) / sizeof(mySuperString[0]);\n\nprint_line(vformat(\"(%d:%d)  Normal : %f : %f, Utf: %f : %f\", iterations, size, latins, latins / size, utfs,  utfs / size));\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564688199/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]